# HISTORY.md is an append-at-the-top log: every entry is a contiguous block
# inserted directly under the `---`, so two agents recording a decision on the
# same day conflict at that anchor every single time, and the resolution is
# always "keep both blocks". A union merge performs exactly that resolution
# and stops interrupting a rebase to ask for it.
#
# What union merge cannot do is notice that two sides edited the SAME existing
# entry -- it keeps both versions of the changed lines, silently. That is rare
# here (entries are written once and not revisited) and is the price of the
# rule; a conflicting edit to an OLD entry is worth reading the file after.
HISTORY.md merge=union
